{{also|Klick}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{homophones|lang=en|click|clique}}

===Etymology 1===
* Most likely a pseudo-condensed pronunciation of {{term|kilometer|lang=en}}.
* Possibly onomatopoeic of the sound of a military odometer.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|slang|military|lang=en}} A [[kilometer]].
#* '''2002''', [[w:Robert J. Sawyer|Robert J. Sawyer]], ''Hominids''
#*: an asteroid between one and three kilometers wide had slammed into the ground at fifteen '''klicks''' per second.
# {{context|slang|usually plural|lang=en}} [[kilometre|Kilometres]] per [[hour]].

=====Usage notes=====
Klick is most commonly used in most English speaking countries outside the USA as a slang word for kilometre.  
Though kilometers are not commonly used to measure distance in the USA, {{term||klick|lang=en}} is commonly used by the US military, which uses the metric system almost exclusively in order to facilitate communication with allied forces.

